      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);">
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Implant vs. Bridge</h3>
        <p>A bridge spans the gap by crowning the adjacent teeth. An implant stands on its own — no healthy tooth structure is sacrificed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Implant vs. Partial Denture</h3>
        <p>Partial dentures rest on the gum and can shift. An implant-supported replacement is fixed in place and requires no clips or clasps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Implant vs. Nothing</h3>
        <p>Doing nothing after losing a tooth allows the jawbone to shrink. Implants preserve bone volume the way a natural root does.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

